    {
      "id": "library/10665-107919/blocks/prose-sec-001",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Executive summary",
      "pageStart": 6,
      "pageEnd": 8,
      "target": "../sections/sec-001-executive-summary.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The Ministerial Forum on TB was organized on 22 October 2007 in Berlin, Germany. \nIt expressed the political commitment of all Member States to fight TB and address \nthe threat of multidrug-resistant (MDR-) and extensively drug-resistant (XDR-) TB in \nthe WHO European Region – the highest rates in the world. Four mechanisms are \navailable to translate the commitment taken in Berlin into action:  \n• the Global Plan to Stop TB 2006–2015 and the Stop TB Strategy;  \n• the Plan to Stop TB in 18 High-priority Countries in the WHO European \nRegion, 2007–2015;  \n• the Framework Action Plan to fight TB",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Summarizes the Wolfheze 2008 meeting, starting from the Berlin Ministerial Forum on TB in 2007 and the four mechanisms for turning its commitments into action, including the Stop TB Strategy and regional and EU plans. It reports discussions on follow-up of the Berlin Declaration, scaling up responses to multidrug-resistant TB, TB in migrants and rapid diagnostics. It ends with agreement that a review of TB elimination like that done for the Netherlands would be useful in other low-incidence countries, with ECDC and WHO involvement.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/10665-107919/blocks/prose-sec-002",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Introduction",
      "pageStart": 8,
      "pageEnd": 9,
      "target": "../sections/sec-002-introduction.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Wolfheze is a workshop and a movement named after a small village near Arnhem in \nthe Netherlands, where in 1990 Koninklijke Nederlandse Centrale Vereniging tot \nbestrijding der tuberculose (KNCV – Dutch Tuberculosis (TB) Foundation) organized \nthe first workshop for national TB programme (NTP) managers of low-TB-prevalence \ncountries in western Europe. The Wolfheze workshops have been organized annually \nin the Netherlands to develop policies, promote implementation and ensure \nmonitoring and evaluation of TB control and elimination interventions. Technical and \nfinancial contributions have b",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Introduces the Wolfheze workshops, an annual meeting series begun in 1990 by the Dutch Tuberculosis Foundation for TB programme managers in low-prevalence western European countries, and their expansion with WHO and partner support. It explains that the 2008 event combined the NTP managers meeting with the workshop and that the surveillance correspondents meeting is reported separately.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/10665-107919/blocks/prose-sec-003",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Objectives of the meeting",
      "pageStart": 9,
      "pageEnd": 10,
      "target": "../sections/sec-003-objectives-of-the-meeting.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Wolfheze 2008 represented an excellent opportunity to have an extended forum for \ndiscussion on the challenges and opportunities shared by all countries in the Region to \nfurther the work to meet the targets of Millennium Development Goal 6, by the year \n2015, through preventing multidrug-resistant (MDR-) and extensively drug-resistant \n(XDR-) TB. \n \nThe specific objectives of the 8th NTP Managers Meeting and the 13th Wolfheze \nWorkshop were: \n• To review the Berlin Declaration on TB and make recommendations on how \nto enhance its use as an advocacy tool; \n• To review the Plan to stop TB in 18",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Sets out the objectives of the 2008 meeting, including reviewing the Berlin Declaration as an advocacy tool and the plan to stop TB in 18 high-priority European countries, in the context of the Millennium Development Goal targets. It also states the aim of the surveillance correspondents meeting to understand new regional coordination arrangements.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
